.TH WEACT-FS35-FEATURES 1 "October 2026" "0.6.0~stage6.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
weact-fs35-features \- guarded one-shot FS35 feature diagnostic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B weact-fs35-features
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Default operation is a dry-run: no display is opened and no commands are sent.
Hardware actions are mutually exclusive and must be explicitly requested.
Both use a preserved connection, mandatory identity, occupancy and exclusive
access checks. No automatic retry, reconnect, orientation setter or Fill.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show usage.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Describe both actions without opening a device (default).
.TP
.B --fastlz-once
Query orientation and require orientation 2 immediately before sending one
compressed 64 by 48 Bitmap at (16,16). Red/green top, blue/white bottom.
Does not change brightness. No fallback to an uncompressed Bitmap.
.TP
.B --brightness-once
Read current brightness, then send one change to 20 percent (raw 51) with a
requested 500 ms transition. Readback failure prevents the change.
Does not draw or automatically restore the previous brightness.
Physical transition duration has not been measured.
.TP
.BI --device " PATH"
Select a matching CDC ACM node or udev alias.
.TP
.BI --serial " SERIAL"
Require a unique matching serial. Ambiguous selection fails closed.
.TP
.B --allow-unknown-occupancy
Explicitly allow the existing limited foreign-process permission policy.
Scanner and namespace failures remain fatal.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Only FS35 orientation 2, 480 by 320. User-tested on firmware V1.0.0.1;
other firmware is not qualified. Accepted TX does not prove visible output.
Do not combine hardware actions. No operation runs during package installation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR weactterm (1)
